{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795390446,"nonce":"wjD4idmkSH5mzFCTfvHqJihE0Sw=","title":"A component of a derivative of a bound view drops its coordinate binding","message":"Found on feat/fvm. With ua = u.bind(x=ra, y=za) (u a vector FEM symbol), ua.x[0] is a plain ScalarView with no _coord_vars, so an expression built from it (a traction sigma.n written component by component) does not know its region; jno.np functions of the bound view (symgrad, grad, inner) keep it. Workaround in jno/_coupling: an interface side with no binding is located by its own Variables (coordinates, normals).","files":null}]}